        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Italian Poker',
            subtitle: 'Card game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Poker all'italiana is a draw poker variant played with a short deck (32, 36 or 40 cards by player count). It has optional blind opening (buio), two betting rounds with a draw in between, and a non-standard hand ranking where flush beats full house and straight flushes have min-medium-max tie rules.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Italian Poker is documented in published rules and active table play traditions.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '4, 5, or 6 players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Short deck of 32 (4 players), 36 (5) or 40 (6) cards from a standard 52-card pack; lowest rank is 11 minus number of players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard deck (short pack), chips for betting; ante amount and min/max limits agreed before play.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "All players ante (invito). Optionally the first player may open blind (buio) before the deal; then dealer gives 5 cards each, one at a time clockwise starting to dealer's left.",
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
