    aiContent: {
      difficulty: 'Intermediate',
      considerations: [
        'Win the pot by having the highest-ranking hand at showdown, or by being the last player standing when all others have folded.',
        'Ante; optional blind (buio, controbuio, over) before deal. Deal 5 cards each. First betting round: pass or open (with pair of Jacks or better, or 4-card straight-flush draw); then fold, call, raise. Draw: each surviving player may exchange 0–4 cards. Second betting round: bet, check, or parol (throw in and carry pot); then fold, call, raise. Showdown: highest hand wins; flush beats full house; straight flush has min/medium/max with min beating max.',
        'Opening requires pair of Jacks or better, or four consecutive cards of a suit (no Ace) that can extend to straight flush.',
        'Flush ranks above full house. Straight flush: minimum beats maximum, maximum beats medium, medium beats minimum.',
      ],
